A||N||4||Springtyme||Adding wing/Removing luggage rack questions||||5||
Z||000000||Springtyme||11-26-2001||09:00 PM||||Alright, call me crazy, but I got a Celica GTZ wing for 32 bucks that i have to sand, primer and paint. Now, I have a luggage rack on my car, anyone have any hints/suggestions of how I can remove the rack and cover the holes up so you can't see them? Also, how do you think a wing like that would look on a fiero? I took the measurements and it'll fit almost perfectly.<P>Guess I'm just lookin for an opinion and help =) <P>------------------<BR>For those of you who don't know, yes I'm crazy.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme_1.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||skitime||11-26-2001||09:07 PM||||Here is a suggestion.  Don't! No,I am only partly serious.  Don't mess with trunk.  Get another one without the luggage rack. (They are cheap and are on most cars in the yards)  Since you will have to paint the trunk anyway, you will have less body work. If you ever decide to go back to original it is only four bolts and you are back to stock.  Have fun.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-27-2001||04:43 AM||||Yup.  What skitime said.  Non luggage rack notchback decklids are a dime a dozen.||||reg||1
Z||000003||falconhulk||11-27-2001||02:02 PM||||Really Monkeyman?  I cant find any.  In the mall here People want $100 + shipping.I am in the middle of switching my rack to a 3rd gen firebird spoiler.  I already removed the rack.  At the moment I just have the screws that were holding it down in the holes.  It actually does not look bad like that.  I am installing a huge 6 pack scoop also so most of the holes in the back are covered anyway.  I think I am going to find some rubber plugs or just paint the screws black.  With the new spoiler you cant see them anyway.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||RedHaze86SD4||11-27-2001||09:19 PM||||I just yanked the luggage rack, filled the open ends of the baby wing and covered the bottoms of the wholes with clear auto tape, filled with body filler and smoothed it all out and it looks factory. took 30 minutes and $6 for the filler.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redhaze1_1.GIF"> ||||reg||4
